  "originalQuery": "A gaming company is using Memorystore for Redis to store real-time leaderboards and user session data. The company needs to ensure high availability and disaster recovery while maintaining low-latency read and write operations. Which of the following options should the company choose to best meet their requirements?",
  "originalOptions": "A. Memorystore for Redis instance with a primary and replica node in different zones within the same region.<br/>B. Memorystore for Redis instance with a primary and replica node in different regions across multiple continents.<br/>C. Memorystore for Redis instance with a primary and replica node in the same zone.<br/>D. Memorystore for Redis instance with a primary node in one region and a replica node in another region.",
